  "body": "Closes #4337, by being much clearer about how browsing contexts,\nDocuments, and Windows documents are selected for each turn of the event\nloop processing model.\n\nThis also fixes an issue where the \"report the duration of the update\nthe rendering step\" referenced the out-of-scope variable \"docs\".\n\n/cc @npm1, who has been helping with this section a bit.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5397/webappapis.html\" title=\"Last updated on Mar 26, 2020, 2:40 PM UTC (8d5651c)\">/webappapis.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5397/81affbe...8d5651c/webappapis.html\" title=\"Last updated on Mar 26, 2020, 2:40 PM UTC (8d5651c)\">diff</a> )",
